> # WHY THIS IMAGE CANNOT YET BE REBUILT ONTO THEIR CURRENT HEAD (measured on
> # m910q, 2026-09-08, three attempts).
> #
> # Their SOAP commit 3f9a062 -- the one that would turn wow-tortoise's operations
> # block from `attach` into a real command channel -- ships gsoap as a PREBUILT
> # static library, `dep/lib/gsoap/libgsoap++.a`, and `src/mangosd/CMakeLists.txt`
> # links that path directly. Two things follow, and both were measured:
> #
> #   1. The archive was compiled against glibc >= 2.38. Linking it here fails
> #      after ~39 minutes with hundreds of `undefined reference to 'strlcpy'`
> #      (glibc 2.38) and `'__isoc23_strtoul'` (the C23 ABI, same release). This
> #      image builds on ubuntu:22.04, which is glibc 2.35.
> #
> #   2. Building gsoap from the source beside it does NOT work either, which is
> #      the non-obvious half. `dep/include/gsoap/stdsoap2.h` is 2.8.125 and was
> #      added by that same commit; `dep/src/gsoap/stdsoap2.cpp` is 2.7.15 and was
> #      last touched by an unrelated one. Wiring the source in (add_subdirectory
> #      plus linking the target) applies cleanly and then fails in 29 seconds on
> #      `'struct soap_blist' has no member named 'ptr'`, `soap_dime_forward was
> #      not declared`, and a dozen more of the same shape: a 2.7 implementation
> #      against a 2.8 header.
> #
> # So the workaround is a base-image bump, and it was MEASURED on m910q the same
> # night rather than left as a guess. Building this exact Dockerfile with both
> # stages on `ubuntu:24.04` (glibc 2.39, GCC 13) SUCCEEDS in 46 minutes, and the
> # binary it produces really does carry the interface:
> #
> #     ns1__executeCommand, soap_serve, urn:MaNGOS, SOAP.Enabled
> #     objdump -T ... | GLIBC_2.38   <- the floor their archive imposes
> #
> # That last line is the whole cost of the decision and is why the bump cannot be
> # builder-only: the RUNTIME stage must also be >= glibc 2.38, or the binary will
> # not start. Both `FROM` lines move together or neither does.
> #
> # DONE, on the owner's decision, 2026-09-08. Both FROM lines are ubuntu:24.04 and
> # they move together for the reason above: a builder-only bump produces a binary
> # the runtime cannot start.
> #
> # What this costs, stated plainly because it is a shipped installer change: this
> # game's server image now needs glibc 2.38 or newer, and its C++ is compiled by
> # GCC 13 rather than 11. Both were measured on this exact Dockerfile before the
> # change was made, not after.
> #
> # The other three games are NOT touched. wow-tbc and wow-vanilla have their own
> # templates on ubuntu:22.04 and no reason to move; a per-tree fact is measured
> # per tree, and this one is a fact about Tortoise's vendored gsoap.
